      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given the hyperbolic paraboloid $(x-5)^{2}-8(y+2)^{2}=z+4$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $y=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2}-8(0+2)^{2} & =0+4 \\\\ (x-5)^{2}-32 & =4 \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $x=-1$ and $x=11.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-1,0,0)$ and $(11,0,0).$",
